{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot motion and perception as a single automaton, capturing the interaction between motion commands and obstacle sensor events. The specification enforces safe, conservative exploration: random_walk is used in clear states for coverage, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end obstacle situations. All obstacle events force a recovery turn before returning to exploration. The design avoids oscillations and infinite loops, and ensures steady progress with reliable collision avoidance.",
  "strategy": [
    "Combine motion and perception into a single plant automaton for clarity and determinism.",
    "Specification enforces: random_walk in clear/search, move_forward in short progress, rotate_clockwise for obs_front/obs_left, rotate_counterclockwise for obs_right, and full_rotate only as last-resort recovery."
